MIMIC implements the Redis serialization protocol (RESP) so that existing Redis
clients can talk to it. Redis is a registered trademark of Redis Ltd.; MIMIC is
not affiliated with or endorsed by Redis Ltd.

Portions derived from Redis
---------------------------

Some functions in MIMIC are ports of Redis 7.0 source code (C, translated to
TypeScript). Redis 7.0 is licensed under the BSD 3-Clause license; its
copyright notices and license text are in licenses/redis-BSD-3-Clause.txt, and
those portions remain under that license:

  * src/util.ts, globMatch(): port of stringmatchlen() from Redis' util.c,
    including its protections against CVE-2022-36021.
    Copyright (c) 2009-2012, Salvatore Sanfilippo.

  * src/resp/parser.ts, splitArgs(): port of sdssplitargs() from Redis' sds.c.
    Copyright (c) 2006-2015, Salvatore Sanfilippo; Copyright (c) 2015,
    Oran Agra; Copyright (c) 2015, Redis Labs, Inc.

  * src/keyspace.ts, the SCAN cursor: the reverse-binary iteration of
    dictScan() from Redis' dict.c, an algorithm designed by Pieter Noordhuis.
    Copyright (c) 2006-2012, Salvatore Sanfilippo.

Other parts follow Redis' documented behaviour without porting its code: the
active expiry cycle (modelled on activeExpireCycle() in expire.c), integer
parsing with string2ll() rules, the order of argument checks, and error
messages and reply formats, which match Redis' so that clients behave the
same. Thanks to Salvatore Sanfilippo and the Redis contributors.
